    <instance moduleIdRef="NoteModuleID" modelIndex="902" path="note.fzp">
      <title>3-PIXEL FLEXIBLE LED STRIP</title>
      <text>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style="font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;3-PIXEL FLEXIBLE LED STRIP&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;3 WS2812B LEDs on flexible PCB. Wire the DIN end; arrows point toward DOUT. GPIO5 → R1 (330 Ω) → DIN. BAT → +5V; GND → GND. DOUT unused. Match pad labels on your strip. BAT is battery voltage.&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text>
      <views>
        <breadboardView layer="breadboardNote">
          <geometry x="550" y="205" width="195" height="115" z="6" />
        </breadboardView>
      </views>
    </instance>
    <instance moduleIdRef="NoteModuleID" modelIndex="903" path="note.fzp">
      <title>ADAFRUIT 4899 — 512 MB SOLDERED SD</title>
      <text>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style="font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;ADAFRUIT 4899 — 512 MB SOLDERED SD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Feather 3.3V to VIN; GND to GND. SCK/GPIO36 to SCK, MOSI/GPIO35 to MOSI, MISO/GPIO37 to MISO, GPIO10 to CS. Leave SD 3V3 unconnected (regulator output). Use Feather power, not IMU power. No removable card: download over USB or Wi-Fi. Verify storage=sd, record and download a short test. Stop/save before power-off.&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text>
      <views>
        <breadboardView layer="breadboardNote">
          <geometry x="55" y="465" width="460" height="110" z="6" />
        </breadboardView>
      </views>
    </instance>
    <instance moduleIdRef="NoteModuleID" modelIndex="904" path="note.fzp">
      <title>CHECK BEFORE SKATING</title>
      <text>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style="font-family:Arial;font-size:9pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;CHECK BEFORE SKATING&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Direct LiPo is a bench-test option; the strip&amp;#x27;s voltage range depends on its revision. Test fully charged and partly discharged. Verify JST polarity. Insulate and protect the battery. Crossings without a junction are not connections.&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text>
      <views>
        <breadboardView layer="breadboardNote">
          <geometry x="55" y="600" width="690" height="75" z="6" />
        </breadboardView>
      </views>
    </instance>
